{"id":"mahabharata-5-113","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":113,"title":"त्रयोदशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 113 · Yayati gives his daughter Madhavi","summary":{"en":"Yayati, no longer rich enough to give the horses, gives Galava his daughter Madhavi, destined to found four royal lines, telling him that kings will give him the horses as her bride-price. Galava takes her to King Haryashva of Ayodhya.","kn":"ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಡುವಷ್ಟು ಸಂಪತ್ತು ಈಗ ಇಲ್ಲದ ಯಯಾತಿ, ನಾಲ್ಕು ರಾಜವಂಶಗಳನ್ನು ಸ್ಥಾಪಿಸಲು ವಿಧಿಯಾದ ತನ್ನ ಮಗಳು ಮಾಧವಿಯನ್ನು ಗಾಲವನಿಗೆ ಕೊಟ್ಟು, ಅವಳ ಕನ್ಯಾಶುಲ್ಕವಾಗಿ ರಾಜರು ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಡುವರು ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಗಾಲವನು ಅವಳನ್ನು ಅಯೋಧ್ಯೆಯ ಹರ್ಯಶ್ವರಾಜನ ಬಳಿಗೆ ಒಯ್ಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"घोड़े देने योग्य धन अब न होने से ययाति गालव को अपनी पुत्री माधवी देते हैं, जिसके भाग्य में चार राजवंश स्थापित करना है, और कहते हैं कि राजा उसके कन्या-शुल्क के रूप में घोड़े देंगे। गालव उसे अयोध्या के राजा हर्यश्व के पास ले जाते हैं।","te":"గుర్రాలు ఇవ్వగలంత సంపద ఇప్పుడు లేని యయాతి, నాలుగు రాజవంశాలను స్థాపించవలసిన తన కుమార్తె మాధవిని గాలవునికి ఇచ్చి, ఆమె కన్యాశుల్కంగా రాజులు గుర్రాలు ఇస్తారని చెబుతాడు. గాలవుడు ఆమెను అయోధ్యరాజు హర్యశ్వుని దగ్గరకు తీసుకువెళ్తాడు.","ta":"குதிரைகளைத் தரும் அளவுக்கு இப்போது செல்வமில்லாத யயாதி, நான்கு அரச குலங்களைத் தோற்றுவிக்க விதிக்கப்பட்ட தன் மகள் மாதவியைக் காலவனிடம் கொடுத்து, அவளுக்கான மணப்பரிசாக மன்னர்கள் குதிரைகளைத் தருவார்கள் என்கிறான். காலவன் அவளை அயோத்தி மன்னன் ஹர்யஶ்வனிடம் அழைத்துச் செல்கிறான்.","ml":"കുതിരകളെ ദാനം ചെയ്യാനുള്ള സമ്പത്ത് ഇനി ഇല്ലാത്ത യയാതി, തന്റെ മകൾ മാധവിയെ ഗാലവന് നൽകുന്നു; നാലു രാജവംശങ്ങൾക്ക് ജന്മം നൽകേണ്ടവളാണവൾ. അവളുടെ വിവാഹവിലയായി രാജാക്കന്മാർ കുതിരകൾ നൽകുമെന്ന് യയാതി പറയുന്നു. ഗാലവൻ അവളെയും കൊണ്ട് അയോധ്യയിലെ ഹര്യശ്വൻ രാജാവിന്റെ അടുത്തേക്ക് പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.113; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तः सुपर्णेन तथ्यं वचनमुत्तमम् ।\nविमृश्यावहितो राजा निश्चित्य च पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed so by Suparna with true and excellent words, the king, attentive, reflected and decided again and again."}},{"n":2,"text":"यष्टा क्रतुसहस्राणां दाता दानपतिः प्रभुः ।\nययातिर्वत्सकाशीश इदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yayati, performer of thousands of sacrifices, giver and lord of givers, said this to the pair, as the lord of Vatsa's land."}},{"n":3,"text":"दृष्ट्वा प्रियसखं तार्क्ष्यं गालवं च द्विजर्षभम् ।\nनिदर्शनं च तपसो भिक्षां श्लाघ्यां च कीर्तिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his dear friend Tarkshya and Galava, the best of brahmins, an example of austerity, and seeing that this alms is praiseworthy and renowned,"}},{"n":4,"text":"अतीत्य च नृपानन्यानादित्यकुलसंभवान् ।\nमत्सकाशमनुप्राप्तावेतौ बुद्धिमवेक्ष्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"and considering that they have passed over other kings born of the solar line and come to me, noting their judgment:"}},{"n":5,"text":"अद्य मे सफलं जन्म तारितं चाद्य मे कुलम् ।\nअद्यायं तारितो देशो मम तार्क्ष्य त्वयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Today my birth is fruitful, today my family is saved, and today this land of mine is saved by you, blameless Tarkshya."}},{"n":6,"text":"वक्तुमिच्छामि तु सखे यथा जानासि मां पुरा ।\nन तथा वित्तवानस्मि क्षीणं वित्तं हि मे सखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"But, friend, I want to say: as you knew me before, I am not so wealthy now; my wealth is spent, friend."}},{"n":7,"text":"न च शक्तोऽस्मि ते कर्तुं मोघमागमनं खग ।\nन चाशामस्य विप्रर्षेर्वितथां कर्तुमुत्सहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet I cannot make your coming vain, bird, and I cannot bring myself to make this brahmin sage's hope fail."}},{"n":8,"text":"तत्तु दास्यामि यत्कार्यमिदं संपादयिष्यति ।\nअभिगम्य हताशो हि निवृत्तो दहते कुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I shall give him what will accomplish this task. For one who goes to a king and returns disappointed burns the king's family."}},{"n":9,"text":"नातः परं वैनतेय किंचित्पापिष्ठमुच्यते ।\nयथाशानाशनं लोके देहि नास्तीति वा वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Vinata, nothing is said to be worse in the world than killing a man's hope, or saying 'There is none.'"}},{"n":10,"text":"हताशो ह्यकृतार्थः सन्हतः संभावितो नरः ।\nहिनस्ति तस्य पुत्रांश्च पौत्रांश्चाकुर्वतोऽर्थिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man whose hope is dashed and purpose unfulfilled, though honored, kills; he destroys the sons and grandsons of the one who does not fulfil suppliants."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्माच्चतुर्णां वंशानां स्थापयित्री सुता मम ।\nइयं सुरसुतप्रख्या सर्वधर्मोपचायिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, here is my daughter, who establishes four families, like a daughter of the gods, who increases every righteous work."}},{"n":12,"text":"सदा देवमनुष्याणामसुराणां च गालव ।\nकाङ्क्षिता रूपतो बाला सुता मे प्रतिगृह्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always desired by gods, men and Asuras for her beauty, Galava, let my young daughter be accepted."}},{"n":13,"text":"अस्याः शुल्कं प्रदास्यन्ति नृपा राज्यमपि ध्रुवम् ।\nकिं पुनः श्यामकर्णानां हयानां द्वे चतुःशते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings will surely give a kingdom as her bride-price, how much more two times four hundred horses with one dark ear."}},{"n":14,"text":"स भवान्प्रतिगृह्णातु ममेमां माधवीं सुताम् ।\nअहं दौहित्रवान्स्यां वै वर एष मम प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"So let you accept this daughter of mine, Madhavi. Lord, I shall have grandsons through her, and that is my boon.'"}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रतिगृह्य च तां कन्यां गालवः सह पक्षिणा ।\nपुनर्द्रक्ष्याव इत्युक्त्वा प्रतस्थे सह कन्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Galava accepted the girl, and with the bird said, 'We shall meet again,' and set out with the girl."}},{"n":16,"text":"उपलब्धमिदं द्वारमश्वानामिति चाण्डजः ।\nउक्त्वा गालवमापृच्छ्य जगाम भवनं स्वकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The egg-born one said, 'This gateway to the horses has been found,' and, taking leave of Galava, went to his own home."}},{"n":17,"text":"गते पतगराजे तु गालवः सह कन्यया ।\nचिन्तयानः क्षमं दाने राज्ञां वै शुल्कतोऽगमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king of birds had gone, Galava, with the girl, went off thinking which kings were fit to give a bride-price."}},{"n":18,"text":"सोऽगच्छन्मनसेक्ष्वाकुं हर्यश्वं राजसत्तमम् ।\nअयोध्यायां महावीर्यं चतुरङ्गबलान्वितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In his mind he went to Haryashva of the Ikshvaku line, the best of kings in Ayodhya, of great valor and with a fourfold army."}},{"n":19,"text":"कोशधान्यबलोपेतं प्रियपौरं द्विजप्रियम् ।\nप्रजाभिकामं शाम्यन्तं कुर्वाणं तप उत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Haryashva had treasury, grain and troops, was dear to his citizens and to brahmins, desired offspring and was practicing great austerity and peace."}},{"n":20,"text":"तमुपागम्य विप्रः स हर्यश्वं गालवोऽब्रवीत् ।\nकन्येयं मम राजेन्द्र प्रसवैः कुलवर्धिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Approaching Haryashva, the brahmin Galava said, 'King of kings, this is my daughter, who will enlarge your family through children."}},{"n":21,"text":"इयं शुल्केन भार्यार्थे हर्यश्व प्रतिगृह्यताम् ।\nशुल्कं ते कीर्तयिष्यामि तच्छ्रुत्वा संप्रधार्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Haryashva, accept her as a wife for a bride-price. I shall state the price; hear it and then decide.'"}}]}]}